# creed-report — standalone Spring MVC + Thymeleaf reporting app. Plain HTTP (no TLS/mTLS),
# port 48080, context-path /report as declared in application.yml.
# GOTCHA: application.yml also has spring.config.import pointing at the Environment-Inspector
# demo config dir (configs/application/creed-resource-catalog/), which can override server.port
# (e.g. to 48080) — check the "Tomcat started on port ..." startup log line if 48080 refuses.

### commit diff viewer — home ("/" and "/commit" are the same page)
GET http://localhost:48080/report/
Accept: text/html

### commit diff viewer — explicit path
GET http://localhost:48080/report/commit
Accept: text/html

### commit diff — offline HTML export (self-contained: CSS/JS inlined, renders with no server)
GET http://localhost:48080/report/export/commit
Accept: text/html

### server inventory report page
GET http://localhost:48080/report/report
Accept: text/html

### server inventory report — offline HTML export (Bootstrap inlined via AssetService)
GET http://localhost:48080/report/export
Accept: text/html

### server inventory report — PDF export (openpdf-html: Thymeleaf report-pdf.html -> A4 landscape
# PDF with page counters; attachment creed-server-report-<ts>.pdf)
GET http://localhost:48080/report/export/pdf
Accept: application/pdf

### environment inspector API — full snapshot with the built-in default launch arguments
# (replays Spring Boot's config-loading pipeline standalone: profiles + config.location +
# config.additional-location; no beans, no web server)
GET http://localhost:48080/report/api/environment
Accept: application/json

### environment inspector API — override the launch arguments under inspection
GET http://localhost:48080/report/api/environment?spring.profiles.active=adc,jpa,global
Accept: application/json

### environment inspector API — effective (active) properties only, rendered to .properties + YAML
GET http://localhost:48080/report/api/environment/rendered
Accept: application/json

### environment inspector API — rendered view with overridden profiles
GET http://localhost:48080/report/api/environment/rendered?spring.profiles.active=adc
Accept: application/json

### environment inspector — HTML page (launch arguments editable on the page)
GET http://localhost:48080/report/environment
Accept: text/html

### environment inspector — rendered-properties HTML page
GET http://localhost:48080/report/environment/rendered
Accept: text/html

### actuator — fully exposed (env/configprops with show-values: always; it's an introspection tool)
GET http://localhost:48080/report/actuator
Accept: application/json

### actuator — resolved environment of the RUNNING app (contrast with /api/environment, which
# inspects a hypothetical launch)
GET http://localhost:48080/report/actuator/env
Accept: application/json
